# A/B Testing Experiments

Ongoing collection of A/B testing and experimentation analyses using real-world datasets, covering hypothesis testing, statistical significance, lift measurement, and segment-level insights to inform data-driven business decisions.

Each experiment is self-contained with its own dataset, analysis script, visualizations, and findings. The goal is to demonstrate end-to-end experimentation skills — from framing the business question and designing the test, to running the statistical analysis and translating results into actionable recommendations.

---

## Experiments

| # | Experiment | Dataset | Key Finding |
|---|------------|---------|-------------|
| 01 | [AdSmart Ad Effectiveness](./adsmart-ad-effectiveness/) | AdSmart A/B Data (Kaggle) | Ad exposure drove statistically significant 18.6% relative lift in conversion (p=0.0389) |

---

## Skills Demonstrated
- Hypothesis formulation (H0/H1)
- Chi-square test of independence
- Conversion rate analysis and lift calculation
- Segment-level breakdown by device, browser, and time
- Business recommendation from statistical findings

## Tech Stack
- Python (pandas, numpy, scipy, matplotlib, seaborn)
- VS Code

